"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 and has progressed through several phases, including design, testing, and development, with Omar Jensen leading the development phase. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The project budget was initially approved at $2M, later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses, with an additional $55,000 allocated for a compliance plan. Upcoming plans include user interface enhancements in October, feedback collection by the end of November, and the implementation of updated security protocols (multi-factor authentication and encryption) in January. A celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
